<title>INDIA: India's Oriental Bank to cut prime rate.</title>
<headline>India's Oriental Bank to cut prime rate.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's Oriental Bank of Commerce said on Friday that it had decided to reduce its prime lending rate to 14 percent from 15 percent, effective on May 1.</p>
<p>The bank said the decision to cut the lending rate was taken on Tuesday by the board of directors.</p>
<p>It said in a statement that the maximum spread over the prime lending rate was fixed at three percentage points, which it said was the lowest in the banking industry.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
